-- title:
--   Descent of the supersingular chart to G-invariants at q=2
-- statement:
--   **Data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and write $\kappa$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ — this field is the subfield of $\kappa((t))$ generated over $\kappa$ by the two Laurent series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`, and a place is a valuation subring containing the image of the base field, distinct from the whole field, with principal ideals — and let $s\in W$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $M'$, is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the analogous base change of the level-$(q^2M')$ field attached to `levelH q M'`. Further, $R_0$ is a constant reduction of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting the base field exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, a map on places preserving degrees and orders of functions, and a clause producing, for each nonzero $f$, a scalar $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue.
--
--   Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$ (`hπ`), and write $A_0=A\cap k_0$ for the valuation ring `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`. Fixed further are: a prime $\ell$, elements $\zeta_0,\varpi_t,\xi\in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $x\in A_b\iff x\in A$ (`hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b\in A_b$; the subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, equal by `hH₁` to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) (a kernel of a `ZMod.unitsMap` reduction out of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$) with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0((t))/k_0$ and a nonzero element $j_\ell\in K_\ell$; an element $\varpi_t'\in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, i.e. of the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t\subseteq K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n,m$; $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and $\tau_0\in\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal; a proof `hjK` that the series `jqNModC k₀ q` (the $q$-fold expansion of $j$) lies in $K_\ell$; an element $a_0\in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   **Hypotheses.** *Arithmetic of $A$ and $A_0$:* $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`); `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace`; `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of the given series; $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian local (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); `hκ` says every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary constants:* $\ell$ is prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`), and $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); $\varpi_t\in A$ (`hϖtA`) and $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`), the maximal ideal of $A_b$ is generated by $\varpi_b$ (`hϖb`) and $\varpi_b\ne0$ (`hϖb0`); the integer $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$ (`htame`); $\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`).
--
--   *The rigid level field and the chart:* `hKℓ` identifies $K_\ell$ with $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0$ of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the subfield of $k_0((t))$ generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of that function field; `hjℓ` says $j_\ell$ is the coefficientwise image $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,j_q$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$; `hϖt'` says $\varpi_t'=\varpi_t$ in $k_0$; $y$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`); `hss` says that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   *The point $y$ lies over $s$ (`hover`):* for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose coefficientwise image over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $R_0$-integral, which satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_P(g)\ge0$ at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P(j_q)\ge0$, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every witness that $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, and every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the chart element and the image of $c$ lies in $y$. *Transitivity (`hOrbit`):* every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra which contains the image of $\pi_0$ and satisfies the same "lies over $s$" condition is matched with $y$ by some level automorphism: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` — the condition that $\tau$ reproduces, on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ through the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, tested against every embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and carries $y$ to $y'$.
--
--   *The rigid chart data `hS1` (thirteen clauses, summarised here):* the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension $\le1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal, and $y$ is the contraction of its maximal ideal to the chart algebra; for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q$ over that residue field, with vanishing locus the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with scalars, and equivariant for level automorphisms up to a character value $c$ in $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in the kernel $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ of the character $(g,c)\mapsto\det g\cdot c^{q+1}$, together with a nontriviality clause and a clause realising the same $c$ with trivial $\mathrm{GL}_2$-part; $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is the image of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ pushed into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   *Numerical and deck data:* $1\le n$ (`hn1`), $n\mid q+1$ (`hnq`), and `hn` identifies $n$ with `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the quotient of `jWidthChar q` of the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen` by the ramification `placeRamificationJ M' s`, the latter being the order of vanishing at $s$ of `jGeomGen` minus its value; $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma_0\in\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`), $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (`hτ₀`) preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); $1\le m$ (`hm1`) and $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot w$ for a unit $w$ of $A_0$ (`hm`); $\zeta_c^n=1$ (`hζc`) and $\zeta_c^k-1$ is a unit for $0<k<n$ (`hζcprim`); the series `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in the chart algebra (`hjC`) and its difference with the image of $a_0$ lies in $y$ (`ha₀y`).
--
--   *The crossing data `hR7` (a long conjunction, summarised here):* $\tau_0^n$ is the identity on $B_t$ while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0<k<n$, and every level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the level automorphisms in $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, transitively so, each end being preserved by $\tau_0$, distinct ends being separated by an element that is a unit in one and not in the other, and all ends being localisations of one common finite-type stable subalgebra; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and Noetherian, contains the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has residue field generated by $A_0$, and its adic completion is identified with a crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$, carrying constants to constants, two elements $c_x,c_y$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m\cdot(\text{unit})$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, the function `jqNModC k₀ q` minus $a_0$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$, and $\tau_0$ to an automorphism $\theta_0$ with $\theta_0(U)\equiv\zeta_cU$ and $\theta_0(V)\equiv\zeta_c^{-1}V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end further carries a valuation subring $W_x$ and a subalgebra $B_x$ with separation and integrality clauses relating them to $y$, to $j_\ell$ and to the other ends; and finally a dichotomy: a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, containing the chart algebra and with centre $y$ on it, either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   *Separation hypotheses:* `hR9` provides an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ which meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and at which no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal; `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which no level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ matches with $y$, an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring containing the chart algebra whose centre pulls back into $y''$ along such an automorphism.
--
--   *The descent data:* $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by the level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$ (`hB₀`); and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ consisting of those $f$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** All of the following hold.
--
--   (1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$.
--
--   (2) $W_0'$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ in $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0'$.
--
--   (4) For every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose coefficientwise image over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $R_0$-integral, which satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_P(g)\ge0$ at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P(j_q)\ge0$, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: whenever $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ lies in $K_\ell$, this element lies in $K_0$, lies in $W_0'$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0'$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$.
--
--   (5) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the above sense, and for every $f\in K_\ell$ with both $f$ and $\tau f$ in $K_0$: $f\in W_0'$ if and only if $\tau f\in W_0'$.
--
--   (6) The following hold for $B_0$:
--
--   (a) for $a\in A_0$, the image of $a$ in $B_0$, read inside $K_\ell$, is the image of $a\in k_0$ under $k_0\to K_\ell$;
--
--   (b) $B_0\subseteq K_0$, and (c) every element of $K_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_0$, $h\ne0$;
--
--   (d) $B_0$ is formally smooth over $A_0$ and of finite presentation over $A_0$;
--
--   (e) the quotient $B_0/(\pi_0)$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f) every element of $B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $W_0'$;
--
--   (g) the image of $\pi_0$ in $B_0$ is a prime element;
--
--   (h) an element $f\in K_0$ lies in $W_0'$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_0$ and the image of $\pi_0$ not dividing $h$;
--
--   (i) $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,j_q$ lies in $B_0$ (for any witness that it lies in $K_\ell$);
--
--   (j) $B_0$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (k) for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$, and assuming the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q$ over that residue field is a domain, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_0$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q$ of the residue field of $A$ at $C_s$ — the fixed subfield, inside the Drinfeld function field, of the subgroup generated by the actions $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ of the pairs $(1,\zeta)$ with $\zeta\in C_s$ — such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s`; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; on $A_0$ the map $\rho$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by the structure map of the quotient field; every element $z$ of that quotient field satisfies $z\cdot\rho(h)=\rho(g)$ for some $g,h\in B_0$ with $\rho(h)\ne0$; an element $z$ lies in the image of $\rho$ exactly when its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, every witness that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, and every $f\in B_0$ with $\tau f\in B_0$, the image of $\rho(\tau f)$ in the Drinfeld function field is the image of $\rho(f)$ under $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$.
--
--   This is the descent step of the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame at the residue characteristic $q=2$: the rigid-level chart $(B_t,W_t)$ over the auxiliary level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, together with its ends and their crossing models, is transported to the fixed field $K_0$ of the group $G$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, where it becomes a formally smooth chart $B_0$ with a discrete valuation ring $W_0'$ and a special fibre identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve of level $q$. It is used by the level-descent theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
